@kLjubomir I agree this is most likely page-specific.

> is it possible for me to locally overwrite playwrights inputValue function

That's not possible. I'd recommend creating a helper function that you call instead of `inputValue()`:

```ts
export function getInputValue(locator) {
  const value = await locator.inputValue();
  return value.replace(...);
}
```

---

That said, we can probably add an option to `expect(locator).toHaveValue()`, something like `normalizeWhiteSpace` or similar. Let's use this issue to track this feature request.

The issue can be resolved by adding a normalizeWhiteSpace option, but after further discussion, I felt the approach needed more consideration. This is because introducing normalization may unintentionally add flexibility to value comparisons, which could make the assertion behavior inconsistent with its intended purpose. Unfortunately, the conditions for reliably reproducing this issue remain unclear.

As discussed earlier, handling whitespace normalization separately with a helper function seems to be the best solution for now.

## helper
```ts
export async function getInputValue(locator, { normalizeWhiteSpace = false } = {}) {
  const value = await locator.inputValue();
  return normalizeWhiteSpace ? value.replace(/\u00A0/g, ' ') : value;
}
```

For now, I will close the PR :)
Please refer to the [PR discussion](https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/pull/34818) for details.
